<PageLayout title="Affiliate Disclosure" description="How TechSpotlight News earns money from affiliate links, and how that does and doesn't affect what we recommend." updated="14 October 2026">
  <p>TechSpotlight News is free to read. To keep it that way, some links on this site are <strong>affiliate links</strong>.</p>

  <h2>What that means</h2>
  <p>If you click an affiliate link and then sign up for a tool or buy something, the company may pay me a small commission. <strong>You don't pay anything extra.</strong> The price is the same as going to the company directly.</p>
  <p>Pages with affiliate links say so near the top: "{DISCLOSURE_TEXT}"</p>

  <h2>Who we work with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Software companies</strong>, mostly through the PartnerStack affiliate network.</li>
    <li><strong>Amazon.in, Flipkart and Amazon.ae</strong>, for some gadget-related links. As an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases.</li>
    <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> may show ads on this site in future.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it doesn't change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>I only recommend tools I've tested and believe are worth your time.</li>
    <li>A higher commission never earns a higher ranking.</li>
    <li>I point out the downsides of every tool, including the ones that pay.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Affiliate links on this site are marked for search engines as sponsored. Questions? <a href="/contact/">Ask me</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
